# This project is written on a Mac, maintained from a PC and deployed in a
# Linux container. Normalising every text file to LF in the repository keeps a
# checkout on either machine from rewriting whole files, and keeps CRLF out of
# the image. Working copies still get their native endings, so nothing changes
# in an editor on Windows.
* text=auto

# Line endings are the point of these two, so they are pinned rather than
# guessed: a shell script or a Dockerfile with CRLF fails inside the container.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
